    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Feature Description\n\nOn Windows, standalone shell terminals always launch whichever shell the daemon finds first in a **hardcoded probe order** \u2014 `pwsh.exe` \u2192 `powershell.exe` \u2192 `ComSpec` \u2192 `cmd.exe`. There is no way for the user to choose a different default shell, and **Git Bash is never considered at all**.\n\nRequested: a user-facing option (app setting and/or per-terminal picker) to select the default shell for standalone terminals, with Git Bash as a first-class choice alongside PowerShell / cmd.\n\n## Current behavior (code anchors)\n\n- `backend/internal/service/shellterm/loginshell.go` \u2014 `resolveUserLoginShell()` \u2192 `resolveWindowsShell()`: hardcoded candidate list `[\"pwsh.exe\", \"powershell.exe\"]` then `ComSpec`/`cmd.exe` fallback. No user preference is consulted, no Git Bash probe (e.g. `C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\bash.exe`), no override hook.\n- `backend/internal/httpd/controllers/dto.go` \u2014 `OpenShellTerminalInput` has no shell/shellPath field, so `POST /api/v1/shell-terminals` cannot express a shell choice per open request either.\n- `frontend/src/main.ts` (`runLoginShell`, ~line 635) \u2014 login-shell env detection runs a shell too; a changed default should be honored consistently there.\n- Unix already prefers `$SHELL` (`loginshell.go:24`), which is why this reads as Windows-only \u2014 but note the Unix sibling bug with non-POSIX shells: #3788 (fish).\n\n## Motivation\n\n- Reported by a Windows user who lives in Git Bash: **SahilG** in the `#feature-requests` Discord thread *\"default terminal option\"* \u2014 currently the **most upvoted feature request** there.\n- Git Bash is a daily-driver shell for many Windows developers; getting PowerShell instead makes the standalone terminal pane a pane they immediately `exit` out of.\n- PowerShell-first probe order also surprises cmd users the same way (SahilG perceived \"only cmd is supported\" \u2014 either way, the user loses).\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\n1. **Setting:** add a `shell` preference (e.g. `\"auto\" | \"git-bash\" | \"pwsh\" | \"powershell\" | \"cmd\" | custom path`) to app settings, surfaced in the desktop app's Settings UI.\n2. **Resolution order:** `resolveUserLoginShell()` should consult the preference first; `\"auto\"` keeps today's behavior. Git Bash detection: `where git` \u2192 `<Git>\\bin\\bash.exe` (or `bash.exe` on PATH), launched with `--login -i`.\n3. **Wire API:** optionally extend `OpenShellTerminalInput` with an optional per-request `shell` override so the UI can offer a per-terminal picker (\u229e new-terminal dropdown) without extra round-trips.\n4. **Validation:** reject-with-message or fall back to `auto` when the configured shell path doesn't exist at open time (consistent with the \"must not open something unusable\" rule in `loginshell.go:17-19`).\n5. **Regenerate API artifacts** (`npm run api`) if DTOs change.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n- Environment-variable-only override (e.g. `AO_SHELL`) \u2014 cheap but undiscoverable; fine as a power-user extra, not a substitute for a setting.\n- Doing nothing / documenting PowerShell-first \u2014 rejected: most-upvoted request, and the fix is well-bounded.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Windows user can set Git Bash as the default shell; new standalone terminals launch in Git Bash (`--login -i`)\n- [ ] PowerShell (pwsh + Windows PowerShell) and cmd remain selectable; `\"auto\"` preserves current behavior\n- [ ] Custom shell path supported, with clear error/fallback when it's missing\n- [ ] Preference honored by the login-shell env detection path (`runLoginShell`), not just terminal spawn\n- [ ] Unix behavior unchanged (`$SHELL` still wins)\n- [ ] OpenAPI spec + `frontend/src/api/schema.ts` regenerated if request DTOs change\n\n## Environment\n\n- OS: Windows (feature is Windows-facing; Unix already honors `$SHELL`)\n- Surface: standalone shell terminals (`/terminals` screen) \u2014 shellterm service \u2192 daemon \u2192 ConPTY\n\n_Filed from Discord thread \"default terminal option\" (#feature-requests). Reporter: @SahilG; picked up by @Vaibhaav-Tiwari._\n",
